...was the recent one where I got killed on the Astral Plane for the
first time.

I was playing a Tourist, the first time where I had gotten one to the
endgame.  I had a plethora of well-charged wands (courtesy of the
PYEC), was dishing out beaucoup melee damage with Grayswandir and
another silver saber, had a bunch of potions of full healing in my
BoH, and my AC was around -30.  It was the first time I had arrived on
the Astral without wearing a ring of conflict (I had never found one),
so I had a tame guardian angel for the first time.  Without having
really planned it, I found myself with a cursed scroll of genocide, so
I wrote a blessed scroll of taming, summoned four purple worms, tamed
three of them, then teleported them away.  I heard many heartening
"Burrrp!"s as I trekked towards the altar with Famine near it.  I was
feeling pretty invincible.

I opened the door to the left altar and found myself occupied for a
bit dispatching the monsters that gathered around me, and suddenly I
found myself confronted face-to-face with Famine.  I cursed myself for
having lost track of him, but I let him have it with my wand of
death.  He dodged and hit me.  Twice more I tried to zap him, and each
time he dodged and hit me.  I had become weak with hunger.  All of my
alarm bells were now ringing furiously, as I realized I probably had
one round to live if I didn't do something fast.  I tried to step
away, but I immediately collapsed into unconsciousness.  My low AC
protected me from the monster hordes, but Famine eventually hungered
me to death while I was helpless.

So what should I have done differently?  Obviously I should have made
myself satiated before taking on Famine, and I shouldn't have let him
close to melee range.  But he dodged three freaking blasts from a wand
of death--and me with an 18 Dex.  Even if I had started taking
potshots at him from a longer range, he still may have been able to
close with me.  What's the right thing to do in that circumstance?

Oh, and I almost forgot: I had two freaking amulets of life saving in
my bag of holding.  I had no time to swap one of them out, but perhaps
in the future I'll just forego reflection, if I'm getting it from an
amulet.


